---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHOR_ROLE } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { personSchema, organizationSchema, breadcrumbSchema, profilePageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate, formatNumber } from '../../lib/format';
import { META, avStand, fz1Stand } from '../../lib/zul-build';
import { P } from '../../lib/engine/params';
const lang = 'en';
const n = (x: number) => formatNumber(x, 0, lang);
---
<PageLayout title="Anmeldekosten: who publishes this site and why it exists" description="Who publishes this German registration fee calculator, why it splits each fee into GebOSt lines, where addresses and deadlines come from, what it never does." lang={lang} jsonLd={[personSchema(lang), organizationSchema(lang), profilePageSchema({ path: route('about', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path: route('about', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">About the Anmeldekosten</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <div class="not-prose mb-6"><p class="text-lg font-semibold text-navy-900">{AUTHOR_NAME}</p><p class="text-navy-700">{AUTHOR_ROLE[lang]}</p></div>
    <p>Radif Partners publishes independent calculators on administrative and money questions. This one answers three questions everyone faces after buying a car in Germany, moving house or finding an old licence in a drawer: which registration office (Zulassungsstelle) is mine, what exactly does my procedure cost, and by when must my licence be exchanged?</p>
    <h2>Why another site on this</h2>
    <p>Searching for registration costs in October 2026 brought up guides that quoted a new-car figure that appears nowhere in the fee schedule in force, gave a range “depending on the city” although the fees sit in a single federal ordinance, and let nobody calculate anything. The cities’ own pages are accurate, but each describes only its own counter, in German.</p>
    <p>This site gives every registration fee line by line from the fee schedule in force, with the item number, the online discount and the personalised-number surcharge, and shows for each of the {n(META.bezirke)} registration districts the official address, plate codes and licensing office from the Federal Motor Transport Authority’s directories, with no appointment, account or middleman.</p>
    <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
    <p>Fees: road traffic fee schedule (GebOSt), {P.gebost_stand.en}. Addresses: directory of registration offices as of {avStand(lang)}, with {n(META.stellen)} main offices and branches, and the directory of licensing offices. Vehicle stock: FZ1 statistics at {fz1Stand(lang)}. Deadlines: Annex 8e of the Driving Licence Regulation. The calculations are on the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <p>We are not a registration office, a licensing office or a registration agent. We take no applications, reserve no plates, sell no plates and book no appointments. Your office’s fee notice is what counts.</p>
    <h2>Funding</h2><p>The calculators are free. If advertising ever appears, it will never sit above a calculator or pose as a recommendation, and what you type stays on your device.</p>
    <h2>Why in English too</h2><p>Every page exists in English for people who have moved to Germany and are registering their first car or converting a foreign licence, and want to understand the offices’ German terms, which we explain as they come up.</p>
    <h2>Report an error</h2><p>Does an amount differ from your fee notice, or has an office moved? <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. See also the <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a> and the <a href={route('terms', lang)}>legal notice</a>.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600">Office data of <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-GB')}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
